    // the whole sprite. 0 rad = pointing up/away (its entry pose); PI = pointing down, rushing the player.
    // e._faceAng holds the current facing (radians); the racer eases it from 0 -> PI during its turn so
    // it physically swings around frame by frame, then holds facing the player as it charges.
    /* _faceAng still wins where something drives it deliberately (the racer's turn).
       Otherwise the measured travel angle is used, and PI (nose-down) is only the
       fallback for a unit that genuinely is not moving yet. */
    let ang=(e._faceAng!=null)? e._faceAng : (e._travelAng!=null ? e._travelAng : Math.PI);
    ctx.rotate(ang);
